# Python bytecode cache (e.g. from running/compiling skill scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The client-intelligence review dashboard is a BUILD ARTIFACT, never a repo file.
# `.claude/skills/client-intelligence/render/build.mjs` writes it to the repo root by
# default, and it renders every client file into one page — so it carries client data
# that this repo must not hold. It ships to Lilian as an Artifact and is thrown away.
# Without this line a session (or a "you have untracked files" prompt) commits it.
ci-review-dashboard.html

# A session transcript is client material — never in the working tree.
# tools/export-chat/ refuses to write here, and this is the second lock.
claude-session-*.txt

# Tax-return working papers carrying a client's dollar figures. They are DELIVERED to the person and
# never committed. Not root-anchored on purpose: the natural place to drop one is beside the working
# paper it documents, and a rooted pattern would miss it there.
#
# 2026-09-25 — WIDENED TO FAIL CLOSED, because the narrow version FAILED. The three patterns below
# were each written for the workbook in front of someone at the time, so every new workbook had to
# guess its way into one of them. Zakom's did not: `Zakom_Incorporated_2025_Form_1120S_working_papers.xlsx`
# matches none of the three, and `git check-ignore` said so only because someone thought to ask.
# A spreadsheet in this repo is a client's figures until proven otherwise, so the DEFAULT is now to
# ignore every one and un-ignore the firm's own templates by name.
# Case-insensitive on purpose: git patterns are case-sensitive on Linux, and export dialogs
# DO produce `.XLSX` and `.CSV`. A fail-closed rule that an uppercase extension walks through
# is not fail-closed. (The three original patterns had the same hole.)
*.[xX][lL][sS]
*.[xX][lL][sS][xXmMbB]
*.[cC][sS][vV]
# ...and the firm's own templates, which carry no client data:
!projects/sops/assets/S-Corp-COA-master.xlsx
# (the three original patterns, kept so the intent is still readable)
# Melnyk-*.xlsx
# *-hoja-de-trabajo.xlsx
# *-working-paper.xlsx
